WHAT THIS IS
────────────

  A personal trading system built around discipline-first
  principles. Three operating components: a Google Sheets
  workbook (data + scoring), a deployed web terminal
  (decision interface), and a behavior log (intent
  tracking). Operates in two modes (Lean / Agg) with
  bench discipline as the central control.

  Live terminal:
    https://nomnomsoes.github.io/lean-terminal/?v=629

  Master sheet (this workbook):
    https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
    1L7uwaOWp35FZUo1iphN7aeHXdmk6fUVknGtlnBQN5UQ/edit


PROJECT STATE (AS OF L20)
─────────────────────────

  Code:        v62.9 deployed
  Trades:      15 of 100 capacity used
  Days bench:  10 consecutive (current streak)
  Discipline:  A grade
  Portfolio:   ~$17,258
  Alpha:       +4.55% vs SPY (last measured 1W)
  Data depth: 10,052 rows × 23 months × 20 active
               tickers
  Dock:        71 shipped, 127 pending


PHILOSOPHY (UPDATED)
────────────────────

  Less new. More reps.
  Curiosity built v1. Discipline builds v2.
  
  The system is in service of the discipline.
  The discipline is the system.

  Bench discipline IS the strategy. Not a backup,
  not a safety, not a tradeoff. The primary
  competitive edge is in NOT trading during
  unfavorable conditions, not in capturing every
  favorable one.

  Honor the lens. Question the lens calibration via
  diagnostic data. Never override the lens via gut.


THREE-STATE COLOR LOGIC (OPERATING DOCTRINE)
────────────────────────────────────────────

  RED    → stay away, sit, or liquidate
  YELLOW → look around for signals, default is NO
  GREEN  → floor it

  Same model used by pilots, surgeons, nuclear
  operators. Yellow with default-no biases toward
  capital preservation during ambiguity.


CURRENT 15-TAB STRUCTURE (alphabetical, all caps)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

  ACTION_ENGINE   — automated buy/sell/trim/hold
                     signals, scoring engine output
  AI_FILTER       — AI-driven ticker filtering
  BEHAVIOR_LOG    — every operating decision (trade,
                     bench, research, build, sick, out)
  DNA_EXPORT      — Lean DNA scoring export
  HISTORY         — daily portfolio snapshot
  HOLDINGS        — current positions, avg cost,
                     date opened, market value, P&L
  MACRO           — macro context layer
  MARKOV_CURRENT  — Markov state probabilities
                     per ticker
  PRICE_HISTORY   — 23 months of OHLC + computed
                     fields per ticker (10,052 rows)
  RADAR           — universe candidates and rankings
  RANKING         — composite ranking output
  SHOCK           — credit stress and shock layer
  SYSEXPORT       — system parameter exports
  TRADE_LOG       — every trade executed (date, mode,
                     action, ticker, price, signal,
                     outcome, notes)


THE FIVE-LAYER LENS (CORE TOOL)
───────────────────────────────

  Each holding gets read across 5 dimensions:
  
  1. Stock layer    — is THIS stock in clear pattern?
  2. Family layer   — are correlated names confirming?
  3. Market layer   — is broader market clear?
  4. Calendar layer — earnings, FOMC, macro events?
  5. Anomaly layer  — recent deviation from norm?

  All five clear → lens CLEAR → trade with confidence
  Any blurry      → lens BLURRY → bench until clears
  
  The lens has veto power over score and bus state.
  Score 95 with blurry lens = sit.


THE BUS STATE (ENTRY/EXIT LOGIC)
────────────────────────────────

  Three states per ticker:
  
  ON THE BUS    — already in trend, keep holding
  AT THE STOP   — entry signal active right now
  NO BUS        — no clear signal, watch only

  Combined with conviction sizing in mode-aware way:
  Lean mode: 2-5% per position by conviction
  Agg mode: up to 12% per position
  Max single position any mode: 15% of total capital


TWO MODES OF OPERATION
──────────────────────

  LEAN MODE (default)
    - Tighter signals required
    - Smaller position sizes
    - More bench tolerance
    - Conservative exits
    
  AGG MODE
    - Faster signals accepted
    - Larger position sizes
    - Less bench tolerance  
    - Quicker exits with TRIM partials

  Mode tag goes on every trade. Without it, we cannot
  separate Lean performance from Agg performance.
  This tag is currently being built (urgency item).


TOOL POWER RANKING
──────────────────

  Tier 1 - The Lens: gatekeeper, veto power over all
            other tools
  Tier 2 - Bench Discipline / Bus State: determines
            whether to act on signals
  Tier 3 - Score Engine: composite scoring with
            weighted inputs
  Tier 4 - Markov / Anomaly Detection: regime
            identification
  Tier 5 - Concentricity / Geometric (when built):
            state-space habitat tracking
  Tier 6 - Stress Map / PDE Layer: heat-equation
            stress propagation

  Above all: Discipline itself. The meta-tool that
  runs the others. The system serves the discipline.


DAILY HABIT (5 MINUTES)
───────────────────────

  1. Open terminal at the bell
  2. Read lens across all holdings
  3. If clear: assess actions
     If blurry: bench, no shame, log it
  4. Behavior log entry (date, action, ticker, notes)
  5. If trade executed:
     - Log immediately in TRADE_LOG
     - Update HOLDINGS
     - Tag with mode (Lean/Agg)
  6. End of day: brief mental scan, any overrides?


WEEKLY HABIT (10 MINUTES)
─────────────────────────

  1. Friday close: review week's behavior log
  2. Calculate: trade count this week, bench day
     count, overrides if any
  3. Quick FEEDBACK entry on what was learned
  4. Check alpha vs SPY for the week


